# Project UUID Registration Checklist

When adding or renaming any project content id (for example `uuid-241`) or creating a new `src/content/projects/uuid-<number>.tsx` file, always keep all project wiring in sync.

- Create/update the project file at `src/content/projects/uuid-<number>.tsx` and export:
  - `id` as a `ProjectId`
  - `content`
- Update `src/content/projects/index.ts`:
  - Add the import for the new uuid module.
  - Add the `[uuidX.id]: { content: uuidX.content }` entry in `projectData`.
- Update `src/content/projects/tree.ts`:
  - Add/update the corresponding node under the correct branch in `defaultData`.
  - Ensure displayed title and `id` match the project file.
- Update `src/content/projects/types.ts` if the `ProjectId` union is explicit and requires the new id.
- Verify there are no dangling ids:
  - Every clickable id in `tree.ts` must exist in `projectData`.
  - Every `projectData` uuid entry must map to an existing `uuid-*.tsx` module.
- After edits, run lint checks for touched files and fix any introduced issues.
